      "text": {
        "title": "Am Montag",
        "de": "Die Visite ist am Montag. Er nimmt die Tablette um acht Uhr. Im Winter bleibt er im Zimmer. In der Nacht misst die Pflegekraft das Fieber. Nach dem Essen nimmt er die Tablette. Vor dem Essen trinkt er Wasser. Seit Montag hat er Husten. Ab Freitag ist er zu Hause.",
        "en": "The ward round is on Monday. He takes the tablet at eight o'clock. In winter he stays in the room. At night the nurse takes the temperature. After the meal he takes the tablet. Before the meal he drinks water. He has had a cough since Monday. From Friday he is at home."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "grammar",
      "type": "grammar",
      "label": "Grammar",
      "title": "am, um, im",
      "practice": "choose",
      "heroTitle": "The time word chooses the preposition",
      "heroImage": "calendar",
      "story": [
        "<b>am</b> Montag, <b>am</b> Morgen, but <b>in der</b> Nacht. <b>um</b> acht Uhr. <b>im</b> Winter, <b>im</b> Mai.",
        "<b>vor</b> and <b>nach</b> take the dative: vor dem Essen, nach dem Essen.",
        "<b>seit</b> Montag means it started then and is still true. <b>ab</b> Freitag means it will start then. <b>von</b> Montag <b>bis</b> Freitag is the whole span."
      ],
      "questionRule": "Day or part of the day: am. Clock: um. Month or season: im. Night: in der.",
